  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapisign v2.0\n\t\t&#39;How to&#39;\n\n### Single document upload in Capisign\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 17 Jul, 2023 at  1:29 PM\n\n\t\tTo upload a document in Capium to be signed. \n\nPlease Note:\n\nCapiSign only PDF files to be e-signed. \n\nWhen signing from a smartphone, please use the landscape mode.\n\nHelp/Guide\n\nNavigation: Capisign > Sign Documents > Sign & Send > Upload Document\n\nFollowing navigation process, a user is able to upload a document into Capisign module to get it signed by client. \n\nOnce performed, a user is able to select a file from the list and upload it into the system as shown above.\n\nOnce processed, a user is required to click the “Next button” to upload a document.\n\nOnce performed, a user is required to add signatories to perform the upload.\n\nOnce it has been done, a user is able to drag across relevant tags, add or delete signatories and review the document.\n\nOnce performed, a user is able to add a message to Signatories, set reminders and send a document to a client.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
